  "body": "Stacked on #3353 (merge #3353 first).\n\nThis PR is the review fix of #3353 that the second read asked for (comment 7077845657 on #3353). I could not push to the #3353 branch, so it comes as a stacked PR. It keeps everything of #3353 (the type, the field, the project key, the MCP door, the UI row and its pins). It replaces only the ring law of Inside and Outside.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New modules `crates/motion/src/machining2d/sided_rings.rs` (the rings) and `sided_chain.rs` (the passes and lead-ins). Inside and Outside no longer sort the closed rings of the area. Ring `j` is now a level curve of the START SIDE alone:\n  - Outside: the outer loop filled and eroded by `j` stepovers.\n  - Inside: the holes filled and grown by `j` stepovers.\n  - The parts of ring `j` in the area are open pieces that end on the far wall. Ring `j` is cut before ring `j + 1`. The far wall loops are cut last, whole.\n- Each component of the area (an outer loop with its holes) is planned alone. Inside on a component with no hole keeps the core-first order.\n- Climb keeps the uncut material on the right (#1555). The far wall ring uses the Auto ring law.\n- A new pass starts with a short lead-in from a piece that this level already cut (at most 1.5 stepovers). The entry then lands in a cleared column, not on the part wall in uncut stock.\n- Open pieces stop 50 um short of the far wall. Without this, the micron lattice put piece ends a hair across the wall ring, and the verifier reported 141 feed crossings on fig8.\n- Refusals by name: a piece with an inner vertex outside the area, and a hole with no enclosing outer loop.\n- Auto: `waterline_passes` is back to the `upstream/main` text, byte for byte. `PassStart::rank` is removed.\n- `start_wall_note` (motion) and one line in `generate.rs`: a level that must start on a wall gets a toolpath note. This is Inside on an area with a hole, or Outside where the outer boundary is in the stock (a closed pocket).\n- Texts corrected: the decision file, the UI hint, and the guide no longer say \"no ring is a full slot\" for all cases. They name the start-on-a-wall case.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe rank of #3353 sorted whole closed loops by winding. After a band splits, one piece loop has arcs on the stock side and arcs on the part side. The part-side arcs then cut uncut stock on both sides: a full slot. No order of closed loops can fix this. The level curves of one side do not have the problem.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (red on the #3353 head 59b42c727, green now):\n- `pass_start_engagement::outside_on_a_split_band_never_slots`. Red text: `climb true: Outside cuts 8.03 mm wide near Point2 { x: 22.34161637316847, y: -5.446639271441037 }`. It is the 100 x 40 / radius 15 band of the second read. A 0.25 mm material grid measures the worst width of cut over any 3 tool radii of floor feed. Limit: 1.5 stepovers. It also checks that no stock is left off the part wall.\n- `pass_start_engagement::outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock`: red on #3353 (52.75 mm2 of stock cut by later entries).\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_outside_offset_never_slots_along_a_level` (fig8.step, EM-0800-4FL, the maintainer's heights). It checks the width along each level, no `Crossing` warning, and no start-wall note on the band.\n\nOther new tests: `outside_on_a_figure_eight_band_never_slots`, `inside_on_the_band_clears_the_whole_band`, `auto_on_the_band_slots_so_the_measure_sees_a_slot` (the measure sees a slot), and the unit test `pass_start::tests::a_start_on_a_wall_is_named_and_a_start_in_air_is_not`.\n\nMutations (each red, then green after the restore):\n1. The #3353 planner files back: `outside_on_a_split_band_never_slots` red (8.03 mm), `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` red (52.75 mm2).\n2. Lead-in switched off: `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` red (321.38 mm2).\n3. End trim set to 0: `fig8_outside_offset_never_slots_along_a_level` red (`141 feed crossings, first Some(\"Crossing { moves: [36, 1654] }\")`).\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 386 steps, 0 failed (47.1 min). It ran on the tree before the last change. That change moved the chain code from `sided_rings.rs` to `sided_chain.rs` for the 400-line law, with no change to the logic.\n- After that move: `pass_start_engagement` (5 tests), the `pass_start` unit test and `offset_pass_start` (4 tests) pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Auto is unchanged: `waterscan.rs` has no diff to `upstream/main`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (release, `--ignored`) did not run. \"Not run\" is not a pass.\n- Outside with \"Do not touch\" picks (`pocket_avoid_started`) has no test.\n- Inside has no engagement pin: its first ring is on the part wall, which is a full-width cut by design. The note names it.\n- A part with a deep concave notch that faces away from the start side. The fig8 waist is covered.\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` is not changed. My session could not edit it. Its claim (\"with an Outside containment the stock edge, so no ring slots the stock\") is true with this fix.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3353: the same functions (`plan_passes_from`, `PassStart`, the 2D Offset arm of `generate.rs`). This PR is stacked on it.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside/Outside cut level curves of the start side, so a split band never cuts a full-width slot; each new pass leads in from cut stock, and a start on a wall is named in the toolpath notes.\n\nRefs #1448\nFixes #3316\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
